<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33632" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῖνος</span>,
			ἡ, <u>Eleusis</u>, an old city of
		Attica, sacred to Demeter and Cora, first in <i><span class="en">
			<u>h.Cer.</u>
			97
		</span></i>; late <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					9.1.12
				</span></i>
			 codd. (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.1.20
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Advs. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσῖνι</span></b> 
			<i>at Eleusis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.76.10
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.4
			</span></i>, etc.; later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1028.11
			</span></i>, al.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσῖνάδε</span></b> 
			<i>to Eleusis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				12.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.4.24
			</span></i>:<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσῑνόθεν</span></b> 
			<i>from Eleusis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.45
			</span></i>.</div>
